Given the details and the code you provided, the potential source of the deadlock may be traced to the missed “await” or “yields” points in the channel send operation. Here’s an analysis of the critical areas related to possible deadlocks:

Line 50:
```rust
// Line 50: Send event without awaiting the send operation
//let _ = processor.tx.send(PaymentEvent::Processed { amount });
```
This call to `send` is not awaited. If the channel is full and the thread currently running this task is unable to send to the channel, it will block. At the same time, the tasks waiting on the `ProcessorState lock` (Line 42) cannot proceed because the task holding the lock is blocked in the meantime.

